# Documentation Rules

- Add JSDoc comments only where they improve code readability.
- Document exported functions, classes, controllers, services, repositories, and middleware with non-trivial logic.
- Do not add JSDoc to simple getters, setters, or obvious private helper functions.
- Use the following format:

/**
 * Brief description of what the function does.
 *
 * @param paramName Description of the parameter.
 * @returns Description of the return value.
 * @throws ErrorType When applicable.
 */